    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "For our study of 120 adipose biopsies covering 18,000 genes, I want to learn how strongly the coordinated expression between pairs of genes shifts with BMI and age, each recorded as a number per donor. That would let us argue that obesity rewires gene coordination. I have the expression matrix and a per-donor table of those numbers."
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "What I understood you are asking for:\n1. \"I want to learn how strongly the coordinated expression between pairs of genes shifts with BMI and age, each recorded as a number per donor.\" -- available from COBRA.\n2. \"For our study of 120 adipose biopsies covering 18,000 genes\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set.\n3. \"That would let us argue that obesity rewires gene coordination.\" -- I couldn't match this to anything a registered NetZoo workflow produces or lets you set.\n\nSelected path: **COBRA**.\n\n**COBRA** — Model covariate-associated gene co-expression with COBRA. COBRA models co-expression as a function of sample covariates through conditional covariance estimation. Correcting gene means alone may leave covariance confounding. Covariate-associated components are not TF-to-gene regulatory edges or proof that a covariate causes the expression pattern.\n\nRequired workflow inputs:\n\n- `expression_file`: expression matrix\n- `design_file`: sample covariate design matrix\n\nOutputs:\n\n- `coexpression_network`: Inferred gene-to-gene associations.\n\nAsk for the workflow's controls and defaults if you want to set them.\n\nThis is workflow guidance only; no execution was authorized. No files were inspected and no analysis ran."
    }
  ],
